the iPhone 11 Pro has been out for about  four months now  and it's clear that a lot of people are  happy with it even a lot of those who  are initially disappointed with the new  iPhone have now changed their minds and  a lot of Android users have actually  gained a newfound respect for this  year's iPhones so in this video I'm  gonna talk about what caused the iPhone  11 pro and pro max to gain so much  traction after people started getting  their hands on it and I'll also mention  my personal thoughts after using the  iPhone 11 Pro max for four months  including the features that matter the  most to me in a couple of  disappointments as well there's actually  one feature that it honestly didn't care  much for before I received my pro max  but quickly became the most important  feature hands down of the iPhone 11 Pro  I'll talk about that feature in a moment  but let's get into what makes this  year's Apple flagship so special first  off the most controversial change was  the design from the front you honestly  can't tell the difference between last  year's iPhone in the 11pro but the back  is where we got some huge changes the  biggest one is of course the new glass  square camera bump that's fitted with  three large camera bumps in an array  that's never been seen before on any  smartphone and even if you think it  looks ugly you've got to admit that it  stands out from the crowd if you see  this triple camera bump you know it's  the iPhone 11 Pro and honestly that's a  big reason why is doing so well I  personally love the design as soon as I  got my hands on it and saw it in person  to me it just looks very solid in  premium another change is the new matte  glass which after four months I'm  extremely happy about my previous iPhone  tennis max started developing micro  scratches on the back glass from regular  use and so far it seems like the matte  finish has actually been protecting my  11 Pro Max from those same scratches  which is very surprising I also thought  that the matte finish would make it feel  very slick in my hands and make it  easier to drop but thanks to the glossy  stainless steel frame I haven't dropped  it once this is actually the midnight  green color which is honestly the best  color I've had on any iPhone the green  tint is very subtle but it really helps  it stand out from the Space Gray so  whether you believe it or not the rear  of  new iPhone 11 Pro has actually helped  sell more of them because it looks and  feels different from other iPhones and  that's what matters to people now let's  talk about the internal features that I  believe have made the iPhone 11 pro so  successful the absolute most important  feature of all is the battery life Apple  did say that we get a couple more hours  of battery life with the 11pro but I  think the underestimated it I'm getting  so much more battery life now that I  don't know how is able to get through  the day with my previous iPhone 10's max  it's kind of ironic that we now get a  new 18 watt fast charger in the box  which I'll talk about in just a minute  because of honestly only using an every  other day now with my old iPhone I would  100% have to plug it in every single  night to make sure I would get through  the next day but now with the 11 Pro max  the battery seriously gets me well into  the next day and there have been many  occasions where it would last me two  full days if I turned on battery saving  mode towards the end of the second day  this was literally impossible on the 10s  Max and that iPhone did actually have  some pretty decent battery life and  that's why I think it's the most  important feature of the iPhone 11 Pro  it's the first iPhone ever that allows  you to do anything all day without  worrying about your battery life yes the  body itself did have to get a bit  thicker in a bit heavier to fit the  larger battery but the extra weight  really does make it feel more solid and  premium at least to me the second piece  of this battery life puzzle is the fast  charger and although I don't use it as  often it's actually super important now  that it charges so quickly like 50% in  only half an hour I know that I don't  have to be as careful with battery life  anymore  I can use my 11 pro for two days and get  it down to 5% battery life and simply  throw it on the fast charger for half an  hour and be good to go my old five watt  charger with the tennis max would charge  so slow that I'd basically only charge  it overnight so that forced me to be  very careful with my cell phone usage to  make sure the battery would last until  the end of the night with a new fast  charger all of that extra care is gone  and with the 11pro max I feel perfectly  comfortable going to bed with only 50%  battery life without having to plug it  in now before I mention a few  things that I'm a bit disappointed with  let me talk about two more features that  I think made the iPhone 11 pro succeed  the first one is performance which you  honestly don't notice much with regular  usage but it actually makes a huge  difference behind the scenes because the  performance of the 11pro is overkill  every single task including playing  high-end games and streaming video is  very easy for the processor to handle so  because of that it actually heats up a  lot less because it's using less watts  to get the job done and that ends up  giving us better efficiency and better  battery life my old tennis max would get  really hot while playing games and I'd  constantly have to check on the battery  life because it would drain so quickly  and now with the 11pro max it doesn't  get nearly as hot and I rarely have to  check the battery life the extra  performance also gives me a lot of peace  of mind knowing that it'll easily be  able to handle anything I throw at it  without any issues and there's one last  thing the awesome performance does that  not a lot of people realize it allows  for the best cameras on any smartphone  the 11pro is able to shoot 4k 60fps on  any of the 4 cameras including the  selfie cam which can also record 1080p  at 120 frames per second there is  literally no other phone on the market  that can record video this good at frame  rates this high and that's because they  don't have the same processor and sensor  performance as the 11pro something that  also really impressed me was the video  stabilization there was a massive  difference compared to the 10s Max and  you can see it in action if you check  out our iPhones head vs. 10s verse 11  pro camera comparison video the 11 Pro  has also done an excellent job in  photography as well with huge  improvements to smart HDR and the new  deep fusion mode which are heavily  processor dependent I personally notice  a huge difference in white balance  accuracy which was the main thing that I  complained about with my tennis max  now the 11pro might not take the best  photos out there but they're very  consistent which matters a lot to me and  combine it with the best video recording  out there I honestly think is the best  choice for overall camera performance so  those three things the battery life  there  or mints and the excellent camera  quality have been the most important  features to me since I got my hands on  the 11 Pro max four months ago some  honorable mentions would be the  difference in display brightness and  improvements in speaker quality even  though I didn't really noticed the color  accuracy or contrast improving on the  11pro I've definitely noticed that it  can get much brighter than the 10s max  viewing the screen is a lot easier while  out in the Sun and it's impressive that  it doesn't really get as hot as before  while maxing it out I'm also very  thankful to Apple that they've continued  to work on speaker quality and volume  every single year and it's much improved  with the 11pro especially thanks to the  new spatial audio feature which helps  stereo music and videos sound a lot more  balanced than before with that I also  want to get into the things that I'm a  bit disappointed about I'm glad we have  the fast charger this year but honestly  getting sick of the Lightning port  especially since Apple is moving more  and more devices over to us PC like  their Mac books and iPad pro I'm also a  bit disappointed with Apple for giving  us only 64 gigabytes of storage on a  flagship smartphone that costs over  $1000 it's simply not enough especially  since I'm racking up more and more  photos on iCloud while the iPhone 11 pro  is display is amazing I would have  really liked to see it get upgraded to a  high refresh rate display at least 90  Hertz instead of the same old 60 this  would help make it feel more snappy and  smooth seeing as Apple considers this a  pro iPhone it was disappointing to get  the same four gigabytes of RAM as the  cheaper iPhone 11 and even last year's  10s so hopefully the 20/20 iPhones get  at least 6 gigabytes the Apple watch  Series 5 has a new always-on display  which is a feature I've been wanting on  this iPhone for years and yet we still  don't have one and finally the biggest  thing I'm not happy about is the face ID  knotch it's been three years of updates  and we still have the exact same knotch  while a ton of other Android phones have  slimmed it down or even gotten rid of it  completely but even with all those  shortcomings a lot of people are loving  the iPhone 11 pro and it's honestly a  huge upgrade coming from the iPhones  head s-max  mostly for the massive battery life  difference alone so there you guys have  it those are  my thoughts on why the iPhone 11pro  succeeded and my personal experience  with my iPhone 11 Pro max after four  months if you enjoy this video go ahead  and click the circle above to subscribe  and check out our iPhone 10 vs 10 s  verse 11 pro camera comparison right  over there thanks for watching and we'll  see you in the next video  [Music]
 

